    "sentence_translations": [
      "The Fascinating Lips, Teeth, Throat, and Tongue",
      "",
      "Everyone, let’s first say the four characters “lips, teeth, throat, tongue” out loud in Chinese, ..",
      ".. and feel what part of your mouth is used to make the sounds.",
      "",
      "“Chun” means lips. When you pronounce this word, you use your lips, right?",
      "It’s the lips that are exerting energy.",
      "“Chi” means teeth. When we pronounce this word, we need to put our tongue just above our teeth.",
      "The tongue then leaves this position.",
      "When we say “hou”, the place of articulation is very near the throat.",
      "When we say “she”, we simply just need to roll our tongue.",
      "",
      "So when we say the four words of “lips, teeth, throat, tongue” in Chinese, ..",
      ".. we also use the corresponding places of articulation.",
      "Isn’t that interesting?",
      ""
    ]
  }
